from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];s=(r/'wacv2007-v3.tex').read_text()
s=s.replace('It combines a temporal representation with an order-invariant mean-pose control', 'The evaluation pairs a temporal representation with an order-invariant mean-pose control')
s=s.replace('figures/pipeline.pdf','figures/pipeline-v4.pdf')
s=s.replace('Visibility is unchanged. This transformation', 'Spatial normalization leaves the already cleaned visibility values unchanged. This transformation')
s=s.replace('and repeats until it reaches a nominal 60\\% target budget or the sampler\'s guard limit.', 'and repeats until it reaches the rounded target budget of 158 tokens (nominally 60\\%) or a 36-draw guard. Span length and admissible start position are drawn uniformly.')
s=s.replace('Every example receives a new mask.', 'The arms also receive the boost because they contain shoulders, so their elbows, wrists, and hand landmarks inherit that region weight. Every example receives a new mask.')
s=s.replace('It does not guarantee leg context in every time block.', 'The retained token can be a shoulder: neither hip nor leg context is guaranteed even somewhere in a particular window, and an entire time block can be hidden.')
s=s.replace('The anatomical choice is a design hypothesis motivated by gait analysis.', 'In the notebook\'s separate seed-zero bank of 512 masks, the mean target fraction is 63.3\\%, and every joint is visible somewhere in at least 74.0\\% of windows. These sampler diagnostics describe draws from the rule, not realized exposure in the five-fold training run. The anatomical choice is a design hypothesis motivated by gait analysis.')
s=s.replace('The context encoder is a three-layer transformer', 'The tokenizer maps four frames $\\times$ three channels for one landmark (12 numbers) linearly to 96 features, then adds learned joint and time embeddings. The context encoder is a three-layer transformer')
s=s.replace('A target encoder tracks the context encoder through an exponential moving average (EMA).', 'A target encoder starts as a copy of the context encoder and tracks it through an exponential moving average (EMA).')
s=s.replace('The target encoder receives the complete, untransformed window without a loss gradient.', 'Within the context encoder, target positions are excluded as attention keys and values; their output vectors are replaced by a shared learned mask token before the predictor receives them. The per-example implementation retains computations at hidden query positions rather than physically dropping those positions. The target encoder receives the complete, untransformed window without a loss gradient.')
s=s.replace('The center retains 90\\% of its previous value at each update, and EMA momentum rises from 0.996 toward one.', 'Once per batch, the center retains 90\\% of its previous value and adds 10\\% of the masked teacher-feature mean. This center is token-weighted, whereas the loss weights examples equally after their within-example averages. EMA momentum follows a cosine schedule from 0.996 toward one.')
s=s.replace('Five outer folds separate the 41 source identifiers. Within each outer training pool, one split from a four-fold source-grouped procedure forms the validation holdout.', 'Label-stratified five-fold splitting operates on one row per source, then expands source assignments to clips. Within each outer development pool, the first split from a four-fold label-stratified source splitter forms the validation holdout.')
s=s.replace('The engineered-feature baseline computes joint-angle summaries from the cached pixel coordinates.', 'The engineered-feature baseline reads cleaned pixel coordinates. Its intended vector contains six per-side hip, knee, and ankle angle means, three absolute bilateral mean differences, and six per-side ranges. The legacy container has 82 fields, but only 15 columns vary in each training fold along this extraction route.')
s=s.replace('square-root feature subsampling, and class-balanced training.', 'square-root feature subsampling, class-balanced training, and seed 42.')
s=s.replace('The accompanying reproducibility record identifies the notebook-associated run, its registry and prediction hashes, and the script that recomputes the tables and intervals.', 'The companion audit record (\\texttt{evidence/reproducibility.md}) names the notebook-associated execution and separately identifies the corrected verification. It records input hashes and the command for \\texttt{evidence/results\\_audit.py}, which recomputes every table metric and interval into \\texttt{results-audit.json}.')
s=s.replace('Its paired difference from S-JEPA is $0.1314$', 'S-JEPA minus corrected RF is $0.1314$')
s=s.replace('A coordinate from one physical side may therefore enter visible context at a slot corresponding to the opposite side in the teacher.', 'A teacher target joint can therefore remain visible as transformed input in the student\'s opposite-side context when the unpermuted mask treats that slot as context.')
